Chapter Three: Into the mines...

What would your reaction be if you were suddenly assaulted by a major
demon? Galanda's was something along the line of ‘Oh sh**'. Ellora's
was something like ‘grrr...'.

Galanda was struck by the djinn, and she stepped backwards. Ellora had
snuck behind the djinn was biting it. Galanda was still in shock, but
quickly drew her mace. She swung her weapon and made contact. The
djinn struck at Galanda again, but Galanda realised because of all the
armour she was wearing the djinn had not penetrated. Perhaps she had a
chance in this after all...

Galanda struck the djinn with here mace again. The djinn missed.
Ellora bit the djinn. The djinn struck out and hit Galanda, causing a
major wound. Galanda healed herself, but was damaged just as much as
she had healed. Galanda cursed herself for locking the doors, she
wouldn't get out before she was killed. Galanda healed herself again,
gaining lightly more health than was lost. This continued for several
minutes, all the while Ellora biting and slashing the djinn, until
Galanda realised she could not focus her mind sufficiently to heal
herself anymore. Galanda felt little pain now, she was healed mostly
anyway. Galanda striked back at the djinn, and was injured herself in
return. She swung her mace again, and finally the djinn fell. Galanda
sat down on the floor to rest, patting Ellora. She realised that
without Ellora she probably wouldn't have made it.

As Galanda sat waiting for her wounds to heal, and for her to gain
back her magical powers, an idea began to form in her brain. Her quest
would be easier and quicker if she had some healers or nurses along
with her for after fights. If genociding something meant it would
never appear, could a cursed scroll of genocide make something appear?
Galanda knew from tales of others that had escaped the dungeon that
nursed in the dungeon would not follow you though, they would only
teleport away. Galanda decided to save it for later.

After several hours of resting, Galanda led Ellora down to the next
level of the dungeon. This level of the dungeon gave Galanda
absolutely no useful items, except for a normal potion of water.
However Galanda was very confused when she came across a second
staircase leading upwards. Galanda took the staircase up and
discovered a strange level filled with boulders and pits. Galanda took
a couple of food rations that were there, and realised that this was
probably an ancient puzzle. Before she could begin to think of a
solution, a water nymph came up. Galanda swung her mace, but before
she could kill the nymph it still the mace and tried to teleport away,
but failed. Galanda was suddenly hit with an idea. While she thought
it out, Ellora killed the nymph and retrieved Galanda's mace. Galanda
laughed and gave Ellora a tripe ration she had also found.

Galanda had made her decision. She led Ellora down the stairs, and
left her there, with a food ration if he got hungry. Galanda went back
up, and read the cursed scroll of genocide.

"Nurses!" Galanda called out after reading the scroll. There was a
large noise, and Galanda thought that nothing had happened, but
suddenly six nurses appeared!

"Hello," said Galanda to the nurses trying to befriend them. To her
dismay the nurses attacked her!

"Take off you armour, it's in the way," said the nurses, still hitting
Galanda. Galanda grudgingly did so, but the nurses kept attacking her,
and were wounding her quite badly.

"Put away your weapon!" the nurses said. Galanda dropped her mace,
feeling totally defenceless. When the nurses hit, suddenly Galanda
realised they were healing her with every hit!

"Wouldn't you like to come along and help me?" asked Galanda, but the
nurses ignored her.

"Relax this won't hurt a bit," soothed the nurses. Galanda waited
while the nurses hit her, and suddenly she felt more healthy than she
had even before entering the dungeon! Galanda was surprised and
continued waiting. After ten or so minutes the nurses all disappeared
completely, but Galanda didn't mind, because she felt much more
healthy than ever before!*

Once Galanda had put back on her armour and taken up her weapon she
returned down to where Ellora was waiting patiently. Galanda picked up
the untouched food ration and carried on. Galanda decided it was time
to investigate the second path down form dungeon level five. But first
Galanda decided to buy some scrolls from the magic scroll shop.
Galanda left Ellora behind and traversed to the shop, and bought
another blessed scroll of enchant weapon (which she read straight
away), plus two scroll of identify. Galanda then fetched Ellora and
left for the staircase. Ellora right behind, Galanda trekked back up,
then went down the staircase. To her surprise, she was in a huge dark,
dug-out cavern.

Once Galanda recovered from her surprise, she light her lamp, and saw
a large army of gnomes coming towards her! Galanda thought. She was
not ready for that many enemies at once. Galanda quickly moved in a
corridor and displaced Ellora in front of here. Ellora was soon biting
and slashing gnomes from all angles, while Galanda healed her. Soon
the flow of gnomes had stopped. Galanda move forward and kill the few
left. Galanda searched through the bodies, but found no items of
interest, except for a pick-axe. Galanda took the pick-axe, but found
that she had difficulty carrying it, so left it where it was.

Galanda began to search the caverns with the light from her lamp, and
found a few more monster, though not many, along with a lot of rocks
and gems. Galanda reached a small crevice about half way through and
found out that she couldn't fit. Galanda realised she would have to
take off her armour to fit through. As she was taking it off she felt
a sharp sting, and swung around. In front of her was a large bee.
Worse, it was hostile. Galanda swung her mace and knocked it to the
ground, then peered round the corner. She sighed as she saw no more
bees. She heard barking and growling in the distance as she dropped
her armour.  That was not unusual, just Ellora having fun with some
dwarves probably. Galanda saw some gold and reached for it, when a
large sting penetrated her bare back.

"Aaaaaaaaaahhh!" screamed out Galanda in pain, and she felt her
muscles get weaker from the poison. Galanda turned around and saw
about six or seven bees flying in through the narrow crack. Galanda
started whacking them with her mace, but not before being stung twice
more, though thankfully the poison not effecting her. When the bees
were dead Galanda grabbed the gold and squeezed through the crack
again, and quickly put her armour on, then healed herself. Ellora
suddenly ran up to Galanda. Galanda cursed under her breath, why
couldn't she be there when she needed her? Galanda noticed that
despite her rings, her stomach was also grumbling.

Galanda bashed one of her tins open, wishing she had just bought an
extra food ration. The first tin contained spider meat, which Galanda
threw away in disgust. She bashed open the other tin, but it only
contained kobolds. Galanda was very annoyed about this and simply
dived into one of her food rations.

Galanda began to explore again, when she was suddenly plummeted down a
trap door to the level below. Galanda quickly got up, and saw that
this level was much lighter, and turned the lamp off. Several gnomes
began to attack her, but she managed to kill them all easily. Galanda
started walking towards where she could see stairs back up, but was
intrigued by a grey stone. She was picking it up, and adding it to her
inventory, when a crossbow bolt struck her armour. Galanda swung
around and saw a gnome lord several metres away shooting. Galanda ran
over to it, but not before being shot five more times. Galanda whacked
the gnome lord with her mace and killed it.

Galanda was about to leave when she saw something glinting out from
the dead gnome's body. Galanda kicked the body aside and saw a morning
star on the ground, engraved with the name ‘Trollsbane'. Galanda
gasped in surprise. It was one of the legendary artefacts she had
heard about back in her home town. From what she had heard Trollsbane
was a weapon that could inflict huge damage on any trolls. Galanda put
it carefully in her backpack. Even if she did not use it, it should
fetch a large price at one of the shops she had passed! As Galanda
continued however, she felt it weigh down terribly in her pack.
Galanda stopped and thought. Eventually she decided to throw away the
food rations she had in order to lighten her load. She hungered very
slowly, and hopefully could find more food before too long.

Galanda quickly took the staircase upwards, fighting off a few bees in
her way to find Ellora. Galanda was happy to discover Ellora had grown
into a large dog while she had been gone. Galanda called to Ellora,
and they went off to continue to explore more of the mines together...


*To be specific, about 52 max HP healthier :-)

